# @epistemologic/property/docblock_coherent — second of the trio of
# #53 property/fracture bilateral instances at doc-claim altitude.
# Sixth #53 family overall (second-of-trio slot); landed per Seam
# Phase D ratification chain:
#   - `820a451` TICK 1 `shards/docblock.mirror` family-root RATIFY
#   - `3283de4` TICK 2 `shards/epistemologic/liquid_extraction.mirror`
#     sibling family-root RATIFY
#   - `ff53d46` TICK 3 `docblock_grounded` (first-of-trio declarative
#     half) RATIFY-WITH-CORRECTIONS
#   - `9b0aeb5` TICK 4 `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded`
#     (first-of-trio operational half) RATIFY
# Interpretation B canonical per Seam pre-review
# `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md` §1:
# narrative ABOVE `---`; `in` clauses + typed declarations BELOW.
#
# This shard is the DECLARATIVE HALF of the docblock coherence
# audit. The OPERATIONAL HALF lands at TICK 6 as
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent` per Mara spec
# `docs/specs/doc-code-seam-shards.md` §6 (routes via
# `@kintsugi/surface`'s `contradiction` class per compiler-error-
# surface §3.2). Bilateral discipline per recognition #53: the
# property side names WHAT it means for a docblock to be coherent;
# the fracture side names WHAT TO DO when a docblock's claims
# contradict — emits a Tomm-linear-then-reflexive question naming
# the two sites plus the frame at which they bind.
#
# === Sixth #53 family; second-of-trio at doc-claim altitude ===
#
# Recognition #53 (`[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`)
# names a substrate pattern: declarative property at
# `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` + operational fracture body
# at `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>`, bridged by the kintsugi loop.
# The docblock trio (`docblock_grounded`, `docblock_coherent`,
# `docblock_no_extraction_pattern`) IS the sixth #53 family
# expressed as three property/fracture bilateral pairs; each pair
# lands atomically per the #53 discipline.
#
# Trio slot ordering per Mara spec §3/§5/§7:
#
# - `docblock_grounded` (TICK 3 declarative `98664a7`; TICK 4
#   operational `6cb6054`) — first-of-trio, ancestry check.
# - `docblock_coherent` — THIS SHARD (declarative half; TICK 5).
#   Operational half at TICK 6 (`@kintsugi/fracture/
#   docblock_incoherent`) forward-promised.
# - `docblock_no_extraction_pattern` (TICK 7 forward-promised) —
#   third-of-trio, extraction-pattern check.
#
# The three bilaterals are INDEPENDENT at the declarative altitude:
# `docblock_grounded` composes over ancestor-existence;
# `docblock_coherent` composes over pairwise-non-contradiction plus
# below-seam-non-contradiction; `docblock_no_extraction_pattern`
# composes over four sub-checks (superlatives, hedges, citation-
# content-match, claim-size-match). Aggregation into
# `docblock_well_audited` happens at @docblock's family-root
# (TICK 1). Each declarative property's fracture body routes
# independently through `@kintsugi/surface` on the class the
# specific failure names.
#
# This shard imports `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` because
# coherence is decidable only on extracted predicates: `contradicts`
# takes two liquid predicates, not two doc-claim narratives. The
# `in @epistemologic/liquid_extraction` grounds the sibling coupling
# to TICK 2's sibling family-root (`3283de4`); the extractor's
# `extract_predicate` output surface IS the input to `contradicts`.
#
# === Predicate substance per Mara spec §5 ===
#
# The docblock-coherent predicate answers: is every extracted
# predicate mutually non-contradictory, AND does no extracted
# predicate contradict any below-seam declaration on the shard?
# In substrate narrative:
#
#   docblock_coherent(d) ⇔
#     ∀ p, q ∈ extract_predicates(d): ¬contradicts(p, q)
#   ∧ ∀ p ∈ extract_predicates(d), decl ∈ below_seam(d.site):
#       ¬contradicts(p, decl_predicate(decl))
#
# Three composed sibling predicates:
#
# - `extract_predicates(d)` is the plural form of
#   `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction.extract_predicate` (TICK 2
#   sibling family-root) applied across the docblock's extracted
#   claim set. Each doc_claim's citation-side text lowers to a
#   `predicate_shape` (splinter(@epistemologic/property/ast) fragment
#   per TICK 2's typed carrier surface) that the substrate can
#   decide. Extractor body itself is forward-promised per TICK 2
#   `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`; until it lands, `contradicts`
#   discharges at splinter(ast) altitude on the extractor's output.
#
# - `contradicts(p, q)` is the pairwise-non-contradiction primitive
#   at liquid-predicate altitude. Per compiler-error-surface §3.2:
#   two claims both fire success independently, but their
#   conjunction implies failure — Carnielli-Marcos LFI `A ∧ ¬A ⊢ ⊥`
#   in classical logic; in the substrate's paraconsistent framing,
#   the two `holds(gap)` claims for the two predicates overlap.
#   `contradicts` returns true when both `p.holds ∧ q.holds ∧
#   ¬holds(conjoin(p, q))`. The predicate's body discharges via
#   `splinter(@epistemologic/property/ast)` against the extracted
#   AST fragments; contradiction is the ONE rigorous surface class
#   with a derived projection operator (`[ω,ω]` Bateson-bind per
#   curvature-and-tomm §5).
#
# - `below_seam(d.site)` walks the shard's `---` seam and returns
#   the ordered set of typed declarations landing under
#   Interpretation B discipline. Each `decl_predicate(decl)` lifts
#   a typed declaration to its liquid predicate at
#   `@epistemologic/property/*` altitude (e.g., a `type foo =
#   satisfiable | unsatisfiable` declaration carries the liquid
#   predicate "the four variants partition foo's carrier"; a
#   `foo(x: bar) -> verdict` action declaration carries the
#   predicate "foo terminates on all `bar`-shaped inputs given
#   the composed `requires` clauses"). The substrate can only
#   compare doc-claim predicates against below-seam predicates when
#   both are lifted through the same `@epistemologic/property/ast`
#   surface — which the extractor provides at TICK 2's landed
#   sibling family-root.
#
# The two conjunction arms enforce two distinct failure modes at
# distinct Bateson levels:
#
# - Arm 1 (pairwise across `extract_predicates(d)`) catches
#   INTRA-DOCBLOCK contradictions: the docblock says one thing at
#   line M and another thing at line N; the substrate reads both
#   at #-narrative altitude but the two liquid predicates cannot
#   both hold. Failure mode routes via `contradiction` (compiler-
#   error-surface §3.2). Tomm shape: linear-then-reflexive — trace
#   p; trace q; name the frame at which they bind (per Bateson
#   1956 double-bind level-crossing discipline). TICK 6's
#   `docblock_incoherent_body` emits exactly this Tomm shape.
#
# - Arm 2 (doc predicate against below_seam declaration) catches
#   DOC-VS-CODE contradictions: the docblock's claim contradicts
#   the type carrier or action signature landed below `---` on the
#   SAME shard. Failure mode ALSO routes via `contradiction` —
#   this is the load-bearing case for the two-channel collapse per
#   `docs/math/kintsugi/doc-code-seam.md`. The doc channel and the
#   code channel are the same shard; their `contradicts` witness
#   IS the two-channel drift the two-channel discipline exists to
#   catch. Tomm shape identical (linear-then-reflexive); the two
#   sites are (doc-side line, below-seam decl line); the frame
#   at which they bind is the shard itself.
#
# Body discharges at splinter(ast) altitude via the liquid-
# extraction surface's `extract_predicate` output; the operational
# half at `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent` (TICK 6 forward-
# promise per Mara spec §6) emits the Tomm question naming both
# sites plus the frame.
#
# === Sibling coupling to @docblock + @epistemologic/liquid_extraction ===
#
# This shard's `in @docblock` grounds the sibling-coupling to
# TICK 1's family-root (`5c0f5ba` + `820a451` RATIFY): the
# `docblock` carrier the property predicate takes as input is
# exactly @docblock's typed carrier. The `in @epistemologic/
# liquid_extraction` grounds the sibling-coupling to TICK 2's
# family-root (`32a1e2a` + `3283de4` RATIFY): the extractor's
# output shape (`predicate_shape` splinter(ast) fragment) is the
# surface this property's body discharges over. Both sibling
# family-roots are COUPLED via this shard: coherence is a question
# the substrate can only ask at the intersection of the doc-claim
# carrier and the liquid-extraction surface.
#
# This shard also imports `in @epistemologic/property` (species-
# family path) per the four sibling properties already landed at
# that altitude: `cold_compile_within_tolerance`,
# `dark_count_monotone`, `restart_intensity_well_formed`, and
# `docblock_grounded`. The path-namespace pact carries the depth-2
# discipline for all species members.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/docblock_coherent.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/property/docblock_coherent` at species-depth 2
# under @epistemologic per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
# The depth mirrors the five landed siblings at
# `@epistemologic/property/{cold_compile_within_tolerance,
# dark_count_monotone, restart_intensity_well_formed,
# docblock_grounded}`: this shard sits in the same species column
# and is subject to the same path-namespace pact.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per Mara's projection-surface spec `63bdecc` §6 the operator
# must audit its own audit at depth=3. This shard's own docblock
# is subject to `docblock_coherent(this_docblock)` at logical
# altitude. Substrate-honest verdict at THIS shard's state:
#
# - Arm 1 (pairwise across `extract_predicates(this_docblock)`):
#   the narrative above makes claims across multiple sections
#   (bilateral #53 family membership; sixth-family/second-of-trio
#   slot; predicate substance; sibling couplings; path-namespace).
#   No two claims in the narrative contradict at analytical
#   altitude — each section names distinct load-bearing content.
#   Concrete `contradicts`-decidability awaits the extractor body
#   (TICK 2 forward-promise) landing.
#
# - Arm 2 (doc predicates vs `below_seam(this.site)` declarations):
#   the narrative above claims `docblock_coherent(d: docblock) ->
#   verdict`; the below-seam declaration IS
#   `docblock_coherent(d: docblock) -> verdict { \ }`. The
#   narrative names three composed sibling predicates
#   (`extract_predicates`, `contradicts`, `below_seam`); none of
#   the three are declared below the seam — they compose against
#   TICK 2's `extract_predicate` surface, compiler-error-surface's
#   `contradiction`-class primitive, and the shard's own file
#   parse. Each name is either a sibling-shard-side action landed
#   at an ancestor commit (extractor-side at TICK 2 forward-promise;
#   contradicts-side at compiler-error-surface §3.2 landed) or the
#   substrate's own parse (below_seam is a metaprogramming primitive
#   composed against the `---` line). No claim in the narrative
#   contradicts a below-seam declaration on this shard.
#
# Verdict: `both_survive` — the shard's docblock passes real
# survival (analytical pairwise-non-contradiction; analytical
# doc-vs-code non-contradiction) but phantom survival is also
# non-empty (the extractor body has not landed; `contradicts` at
# liquid-predicate altitude cannot concretely check yet; the
# `below_seam` walk cannot concretely resolve typed-decl liquid
# predicates yet). Promotion to `real_survives` awaits: extractor
# body (TICK 2 forward-promise) + `contradicts` discharge body +
# fracture body at TICK 6 + Seam second-witness audit at analytical
# altitude on the extracted predicate pairs. Per Mara spec
# §Cross-cutting: this is the honest verdict at THIS shard's state.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @epistemologic/liquid_extraction
in @docblock

prism @epistemologic/property/docblock_coherent {
  focus docblock_coherent
  project docblock_coherent
  split docblock_coherent
  shift docblock_coherent
  settle docblock_coherent
}

# === docblock_coherent predicate (declarative half) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING PREDICATE. Returns verdict that every extracted
# predicate in `d` is mutually non-contradictory AND does not
# contradict any below-seam declaration on `d.site`. Per Mara
# spec §5 predicate substance:
#
#   docblock_coherent(d) ⇔
#     ∀ p, q ∈ extract_predicates(d): ¬contradicts(p, q)
#   ∧ ∀ p ∈ extract_predicates(d), decl ∈ below_seam(d.site):
#       ¬contradicts(p, decl_predicate(decl))
#
# Body discharges at splinter(ast) altitude via the liquid-
# extraction surface's `extract_predicate` output; the operational
# half at `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent` (TICK 6 forward-
# promise per Mara spec §6) emits a Tomm-linear-then-reflexive
# question (per compiler-error-surface §5.3 Bateson double-bind
# discipline) naming the two contradicting sites plus the frame
# at which they bind when this predicate fails.
docblock_coherent(d: docblock) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/property/docblock_coherent
out docblock_coherent
